Sibling-Safe Face Recognition System

A high-precision Face Recognition Attendance System built with Flask and OpenCV Deep Learning.

This project is specifically engineered to solve the "Sibling Challenge" (distinguishing between brothers/sisters with similar facial structures) by utilizing SFace (Sigmoid-constrained Hypersphere Loss) instead of traditional methods like Haar Cascades or LBPH.

🚀 Key Features

Deep Learning Accuracy: Uses YuNet for detection and SFace for recognition (99%+ accuracy on LFW benchmark).

Sibling differentiation: Uses a tuned Cosine Similarity Threshold (0.50) to strictly separate similar faces.

Real-Time Processing: Low-latency video feed using ONNX runtime.

Attendance Logging: Automatically logs recognized users with a timestamp.

📂 Project Structure

app.py: Main Flask application and AI logic.

yunet.onnx: The Face Detection Model (Finds the face).

face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx: The Face Recognition Model (Identifies the person).

uploads/: Stores the raw reference images for registered users.

features.pkl: Stores the computed 128-D mathematical embeddings (auto-generated).

🛠️ Installation & Setup

1. Install Dependencies

Make sure you have Python installed. Run the following command to install the required libraries:

pip install -r requirements.txt


2. Verify Model Files

Ensure the following two files are present in the project root directory (same folder as app.py). These are required for the AI to function:

yunet.onnx

face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx

3. Run the Application

Start the server by running:

python app.py


Access the application in your web browser at:
http://127.0.0.1:5000

🧠 How Sibling Detection Works

Standard face recognition libraries often use a distance threshold of 0.6 (Euclidean) or 0.36 (Cosine). While this works for strangers, it often fails for siblings, classifying them as the same person.

To fix this, this project implements a Strict Cosine Similarity Threshold:

Standard Match: > 0.363

Sibling Safe Match: > 0.50

The variable SIBLING_THRESHOLD = 0.50 in app.py ensures that the system only confirms an identity if the biometric match is extremely close, effectively rejecting false positives caused by family resemblance.

📝 Usage

Register: Go to the "Register New Face" section, upload a clear photo, and enter a name.

Recognize: Go to the "Live Feed". The system will draw a Green box for confirmed matches and a Red box for Unknowns.

Attendance: Recognized faces are automatically added to the attendance log below the video.

⚠️ Troubleshooting

"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not find .onnx file":

Ensure yunet.onnx and face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx are in the main folder, not inside a subfolder.

System confusing siblings?

Open app.py and increase SIBLING_THRESHOLD from 0.50 to 0.55.